    "title": "Ibuprofen use with renal impairment on TDF",
    "message": "Patient takes ibuprofen 400 mg 2–3 times weekly for headaches. With eGFR at 52 mL/min/1.73m² and rising creatinine on TDF, concurrent NSAID use increases risk of further renal injury. TDF guidelines list chronic kidney disease and acute kidney injury as major toxicities. Ibuprofen may accelerate renal decline in this already compromised patient.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Counsel patient to discontinue ibuprofen. Recommend paracetamol for headache relief. Monitor renal function closely if NSAID use cannot be avoided.",
