    "title": "Fatigue may signal TDF lactic acidosis",
    "message": "Guidelines list exhaustion or extreme fatigue as a presenting sign of TDF-associated lactic acidosis or severe hepatomegaly with steatosis. Patient reports mild fatigue over 2 months. Evidence for drug attribution: fatigue is a recognized TDF toxicity and patient has been on TDF for 3 years. Evidence against: patient attributes fatigue to work schedule, and no muscle cramps, abdominal pain, or decreased appetite are reported. Given concurrent renal impairment, this symptom warrants further evaluation.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
